{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"volumetric flow rate conversion volumetric flow rate conversion","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion.md","fileName":"Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Volume Unit Scaling","Compound Rate Unit Conversion","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"volumetric flow rate conversion volumetric flow rate conversion","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion.md","fileName":"Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion","heading":"Volumetric Flow Rate Conversion","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Volumetric flow combines volume with inverse time, such as ft³/s or L/day. The book converts cubic feet per second to cubic meters per second with a volume ratio because the seconds already match. When the time unit differs, a second factor must be oriented to cancel the denominator as well. The app lists per-second, per-minute, and per-day choices, illustrating why a flow result cannot be obtained from a volume factor alone in every case. See [[Volume Unit Scaling]] and [[Compound Rate Unit Conversion]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific